{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, if you heed.</b> וְהָיָה refers back to what was said above: ״of the rain of heaven you will drink water.״" "<b>And it shall be, if you heed, you will heed.</b> If you heed what is old, you will heed what is new. And likewise ״if you forget, you will forget״ (Deuteronomy 8) — if you have begun to forget, you will end up forgetting all of it; for so it is written in the scroll: ״If you forsake me day by day, I will forsake you.״" "<b>Which I command you today.</b> That they be upon you as new, as though you heard them this very day (Sifrei)." "<b>To love HaShem.</b> That you not say: I am studying in order to become rich, in order to be called Rabbi, in order to receive reward — but whatever you do, do out of love, and the honor will ultimately follow (ibid.)." "<b>And to serve Him with all your heart.</b> Service that is in the heart — and that is prayer, for prayer is called עֲבוֹדָה, as it is said: ״your Elohim whom you serve continually״ (Daniel 6) — and is there temple-service in Babylon? Rather, it is because he was praying, as it is said (ibid.) ״and windows were open for him…״; and likewise regarding David it says (Psalms 141) ״Let my prayer be established as incense before You.״" "<b>With all your heart and with all your soul.</b> But was it not already warned, ״בְּכָל לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל נַפְשְׁךָ״ (Deuteronomy 6)? Rather — a warning to the individual, a warning to the community (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:36.946106387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}